Section Content <code>final</code> The fully merged Copier configuration (questions + directives) <code>layers</code> Per-layer question values (contributions only, not cumulative) <code>states</code> Per-layer cumulative state (requires <code>include_states=true</code> at compose time) <code>deltas</code> Per-layer delta from previous state (requires <code>include_deltas=true</code>) <code>stats</code> Aggregate statistics (see <code>CompositionStats</code> in Data models) <p>Question provenance: When <code>--questions</code> mode is active, each question in the output SHOULD include a <code>source</code> field indicating which template layer originally declared it and whether it was overridden by a later layer. This enables template authors to trace question origins and identify unintentional overrides.</p> <p>Example (<code>--questions --format json</code>):</p> <pre><code>{
  "questions": [
    {
      "name": "project_name",
      "type": "str",
      "default": null,
      "source": "project@2.1.0",
      "overridden_by": null
    },
    {
      "name": "dependencies",
      "type": "json",
      "default": ["streamlit", "pydantic&gt;=2"],
      "source": "project@2.1.0",
      "overridden_by": "streamlit@1.0.0"
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>Question ordering in <code>--questions</code> mode: The question table MUST be output in the same order as the interactive prompting sequence — topological order (base templates first, root template last), preserving declaration order within each template. This ensures that an answer preset file built from <code>--questions</code> output maps directly to the prompting experience.</p> <p>Both YAML and JSON export formats are supported. When <code>--output &lt;dir&gt;</code> is specified, sections are written to the directory; otherwise they are rendered to stdout. File naming within the output directory is implementation-defined.</p>
